# sysutils_systemd_unit (Resource)

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

Use it for units that you define yourself, of every type that has unit files: services, sockets, devices, mounts, automounts, swaps, targets, paths, timers and slices, as well as templates and instance-specific unit files. To change a unit that a package installed, or a scope unit, manage a drop-in with [`sysutils_systemd_dropin`](./systemd_dropin.md). [`sysutils_service`](./service.md) manages whether units that a package installed, and instances of templates, are enabled and running.

